  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe WCS page now shows the existing post refusal instead of an unconditional mirrored-program note.\n\n- Keep a display-only cache in `WcsUi`, keyed by document revision and active setup.\n- Read `setup_wcs_flip::setup_problem`, then `setup_post_problems`, in the same order as the existing status line.\n- Share the result with the flip status. Reuse it on unchanged frames.\n- Keep the mirrored note for a permitted flip. Show no flip note when no axis is flipped.\n\nThe post gate never reads this cache. No command validation, post decision, generated output, geometry, collision check or stock simulation changed. No dependency, NC/CL golden or snapshot PNG changed.\n\nStarting base: `NeoTech/Camcraft main 9b141e1122fad4aca12e6502dd5f4963209b4e68`.\nPR base at publication: `main fc8d8fbd2ebb63fa104648bdc89ac6e9faeb85e3`. The later main changes do not touch the changed WCS files or `state.rs`. A read-only merge-tree check is clean; no main refresh was added to this issue branch.\nSource head: `fe4656c1b166bc1df64bd5a05378831be158a07f`.\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2497#issuecomment-7210382707\n\n## Verification\n\nAll commands ran on Linux with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3` and one build at a time.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: all 18 steps passed; no failure or stall. UI lib: 1,727 passed, 8 existing ignored. This includes `layout_page_wcs`, the WCS page tests and all 10 flip tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/main --only 'motion light' --only 'app light'`: all 11 light twins passed across five steps. The broad release prebuild was excluded; each selected test step compiled its actual target.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib wcs_flip_tests -- --nocapture`: all 10 passed after every negative control was restored.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNew structural pins:\n- `a_flipped_non_z_rotation_paints_the_actual_post_refusal`\n- `a_probe_paints_the_refusal_and_operation_edits_and_undo_refresh_it`\n- `document_rotation_and_post_changes_refresh_the_painted_note`\n- `the_active_setup_is_part_of_the_cache_key_even_at_the_same_revision`\n- `project_replacement_and_new_clear_the_old_painted_refusal`\n- `unchanged_frames_do_not_reload_a_post_script`\n\nThe tests query the real painted WCS page. The file-backed script test changes its manifest on disk. Still frames reuse the cached result; a real document edit refreshes it. Post-selection tests also cover undo and redo.\n\nNegative controls failed as expected: the old page, a stale cache key, a key without setup identity, and cache bypass. The rotated-refusal test failed on the original production source before implementation. Exact-base captures also failed the rotated and probe assertions. All temporary controls are removed.\n\nNot run: full heavy lanes, app posting/catalog suites, release packaging or physical-machine tests. This change only wires UI diagnostics. No post or toolpath source changed. The historical unrelated golden failure in the issue thread was not treated as a current result.\n\n## Before and after\n\nThese are genuine renders of the WCS page through the existing egui test renderer, not mockups or snapshot goldens.\n\nBefore: production source from `9b141e1122fad4aca12e6502dd5f4963209b4e68`, with only the test capture harness added. After: exact source head `fe4656c1b166bc1df64bd5a05378831be158a07f`.\n\nThe same `CAMCRAFT_WCS_EVIDENCE_DIR` test hook captured both pages at the same size. All images live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch, at `8d408e2c70442700bdbd304e1a33f434e845052f`. The source branch contains no images or review evidence.\n\n### Flipped and non-Z-rotated WCS\n\nBefore:\n![Rotated flip before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/8d408e2c70442700bdbd304e1a33f434e845052f/2497/before-rotated-flip.png)\n\nAfter:\n![Rotated flip after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/8d408e2c70442700bdbd304e1a33f434e845052f/2497/after-rotated-flip.png)\n\n### Probe operation in a flipped setup\n\nBefore:\n![Probe flip before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/8d408e2c70442700bdbd304e1a33f434e845052f/2497/before-probe-flip.png)\n\nAfter:\n![Probe flip after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/8d408e2c70442700bdbd304e1a33f434e845052f/2497/after-probe-flip.png)\n\nChangelog: The WCS page shows cached post refusals for flips instead of incorrectly claiming that the program is mirrored.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2497\n",
